# api-routes-errors

> **Purpose:** Keep the API contract strict and identical to docs/api-design.md.
>
> **Applies to:** Routes and middleware in `apps/api`, and `packages/schema`.

## Routes
- Routes stay thin: validate, call a service, respond.
- Routes never call Prisma, OpenAI or Tavily directly.
- Wrap every handler with `asyncHandler`, so routes need no try/catch.
- Match the paths, status codes and shapes in `docs/api-design.md`.

## Validation
- Validate every body, param and query with the `validate(schema)` middleware.
- Schemas come from `@stamp/schema`.

## Errors
- Errors always use `{ "error": { "code", "message" } }`.
- Use only these codes: `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `RATE_LIMITED`, `RUN_CAP_REACHED`, `INTERNAL`.
- One central `errorHandler` middleware formats every error.
- Never send raw exception text or stack traces to the client.
